---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The component's documentation, live rather than a screenshot, and
// anchored at the Example section rather than at the top of the page.
//
// Why the Example and not the masthead: the sidebar is sticky, so it
// carries "Mission Control / Checklist" and the whole section list no
// matter where the page is scrolled to. The identity is already on
// screen, which frees the body of the frame for the one thing on this
// page that is not in every design system's docs.
//
// That thing is the address bar under the specimen. Every state is a
// named value, unknown values are ignored rather than guessed at, and
// picking a state rewrites the specimen and the address together. Say
// out loud what it buys: an agent can open a state and look at it, not
// only read a paragraph describing one. Docs that are machine-readable
// by construction rather than by a second export nobody maintains.
//
// The honest caveat, and it is worth saying before the engineer on the
// panel says it: this vocabulary grew on the prototypes, and it
// documents states the component has rather than being generated from
// the component. The claim is that the property should carry into the
// docs, not that these are generated docs today.
//
// Sizing is measured, not guessed. The Example section runs 840px at
// scale 1, against a slide budget of 800, so `compact=1` drops the two
// prose blocks that get said out loud anyway. Compact measures 709 at
// scale 1 and 779 at scale 1.1, which is the largest step that still
// clears 800. Above that the page also outgrows the 1640 frame width.
//
// The canvas inside the page keeps its full menu reserve at this scale.
// That is deliberate: this embed gets driven live, and centring the
// specimen instead of reserving room below it is what made the row
// menu clip on the last row.
//
// Drive it, roughly in this order:
//   pick two or three states and let the address change under them
//   hover a row, open the row menu, take Move up
//   scroll the page to Props or States if anybody asks what else is in
//     it, and to Open questions if they ask what is not finished
---

<Slide subtitle="Docs">
	<iframe
		src="/decks/2026-checklist-component/docs?compact=1&scale=1.1&state=default#example"
		title="The Checklist component documentation, live"
		class="live-embed m-0! block h-[800px] w-[1640px] max-h-none! max-w-none! border-0"
	></iframe>
</Slide>
